ThefloorMod()method returns the remainder of a division between two integers where the result of the division was rounded down.

SyntaxOne of the following:public static int floorMod(intdividend, intdivisor)public static long floorMod(longdividend, longdivisor)Parameter ValuesParameterDescriptiondividendRequired. The dividend of the remainder operation.divisorRequired. The divisor of the remainder operation.Technical DetailsReturns:Anintorlongvalue representing the remainder from a division between two integers.Throws:ArithmeticException- If the divisor is zero.Java version:1.8+❮ Math Methods★+1Sign in to track progress

### Code Snippets

```
Example
Return the remainders of rounded-down divisions:
System.out.println(Math.floorMod(10, 4));
System.out.println(Math.floorMod(-10, 4));
System.out.println(Math.floorMod(10, 3));
System.out.println(Math.floorMod(-10, 3));
